>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_looper`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_looper :
  string * (simpset -> tactic) -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Replaces all loopers of a simpset with one named looper.

`set_looper (name, mk) ss` is `ss` with `(name, mk)` as its only looper;
all others, including split rules, are removed.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

The looper of `split_ss` splits the conditional; after `set_looper`,
only the conjunction is split.

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val cases_ss = bool_ss ++ simpLib.split_ss;
>> SIMP_TAC cases_ss [] ([], “(if b then p else q) ∧ r”) c;
>> SIMP_TAC (simpLib.set_looper ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC) cases_ss) []
     ([], “(if b then p else q) ∧ r”) c;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_looper`](#simpLib.add_looper),
[`simpLib.del_looper`](#simpLib.del_looper).
